                     recombination in Escherichia coli. The RecE pathway is
                     activated in recB, recC sbcA (suppressors of recB and
                     recC) mutants. Activation of the RecE pathway results in
                     the production of at least two phage proteins relevant for
                     recombinational repair. RecE is a duplex DNA-specific
                     exonuclease which produces 3' overhangs in duplex DNA by
                     preferentially degrading the 5'-ending strands.
                     Recombinational repair of E.coli chromosomal DNA involves
                     as well other proteins: RecA, RecF, RecJ, RecO, RecR, and
